  "partners.empty.body": "Each owner gets one account here. It shows what they have put into the business, what they have taken out, and what the business owes them.",
  "@partners.empty.body": {"description": "S14 empty state, second line: what this screen is for, in the user’s own words (02 §7.1)."},
  "partners.solo.title": "Nothing to show here.",
  "@partners.solo.title": {"description": "S14 when the book turns out to have a single owner. ADR 2026-09-09b 🔒: a *Just me* business never mentions partners, ratios or profit distribution anywhere in the app — so this state says none of those words. It exists only because a stale link or an ownership change can land on the route; the shell never offers it (07 §1 rule 6 still wants a way back, which the app bar gives)."},
  "partners.solo.body": "This book has one owner, so there is nothing to divide up.",
